<Table width="450">
<tr>
<td width="300">
<b><font face="Arial" size="2">
Title: Journeyman Boots
</font></b>
</td>
<td width="150" align="right"><b><font face="Arial" size="2">Date Posted: 6/18/01
  </font></b>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td colspan="2" width="450">
<font face="Arial" size="2">
Mujahid is organizing another Ancient Cyclops Hunt. Those that are at a level that they can survive in the Southern desert of Ro and would like to Obtain a pair of the Journeyman Boots should contact Mujahid. Hunting the Anicent Cyclops is the first part of the quest for the boots, you must loot his Ring of the Ancients. The AC is a very rare spawn in both South Ro and in the Ocean of Tears, but it always drops the ring. Other items you will need for the quest are, 3250 gold pieces and a shadowed sythe. The sythe is a no rent item so it must be obtained last. You give all three of these items to Hasten Bootstrutter in Rathe mountains and he gives you the boots.
The JBoots have a right clickable effect that is similiar to a lvl 14 Spirit of the wolf spell. This effect can be cast while moving, but has the same outdoor only limitations as spirit of the wolf.
The AC that spawns in SRO is level 32 and considered a freefor all mob, this means that you cannot camp him in SRO. It does not mean that KSing is allowed. Once some one engages the AC in battle it is their kill, do not interfear with them. The best way to hunt the AC in SRO is with a large group. Go around killing everything in sight. The place hodlers for the AC are A mummy,Terrotrantula, Sand Giants, Sand Giant Hassan, all spiders, and one little trick is to kill whatever spawns in the undead tower at EXACTLY 8pm game time, this will force a rare spawn. By having alot of guild members spread out in the zone it is easier to spot and engage the AC first. Also the loot you recieve from the many sand giants that you will kill during the process is well worth it.
The AC in ocean of tears is level 44, he spawns on the island next to sister island. He is also a rare spawn and has several place holders. This AC spawn site can be camped. There is also no other spawns on the island, although many players do pull the seafury cyclops over to this island to fight them without fear of another seafury joining the fight.

The only thing we will ask of anyone that comes to the AC hunt, Is that once you obtain your own pair of Jboots Please return to the hunt and help others in the Guild get theirs.
the last AC hunt we held was in SRO and it lasted over 4 weeks. No one forced to come every night, as that is impossible for many, but come when you can. SRO is a great place to make some serious money if nothing else. Lots of fine steel and bronze weapons drop there, medium quality cat pelts,bone chips. If you need water there are wandering waterboys that will give you some for free. Although most of them are very rude and you will find it nessary to kill them, maybe that is why they are called madmen. Food can be purchased at the erudite merchant in the north west corner, he is on solusek temple faction, as is the named orc Ortallius. So don't attack Ortallius, as it will mess up your temple faction. If the merchant wont sell to you, give Ortallius dervish cutthroat rings, 3 at a time. There are 2 derv camps in the zone.
For any of you who are thining about sand giant hunting, this is the zone you want to be in. First off just as many SGs spawn here as in Oasis if your taking out the place holders. Next thing is there is a smaller area to try to cover. Third is the fact that the super high level SG Cazel only spawns in Oasis so there is no need to worry about him ruining your day.

Nuuan
</font>

</td>
